  id: Scene11_FAQ_3
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: Because a hot wire behaves differently from a cool one. If the wire warmed
    up during our readings, the same push would give a slightly different current,
    and our neat straight line would start to bend. Keeping the temperature steady
    keeps the comparison fair.
